# database.sqlite is tracked on purpose: it is the deployed content store.
#
# Production is read-only — Vercel's filesystem cannot be written to — so the
# admin can only save on your machine. The workflow is: edit through /admin
# locally, commit the updated database.sqlite, push, redeploy.
#
# This requires SESSION_DRIVER=cookie and CACHE_STORE=array in production. With
# either left on the `database` driver, an ordinary page view attempts a write
# and returns a 500 (verified: "attempt to write a readonly database").
#
# The sidecar journal/WAL files are still ignored; only the database itself is
# committed.
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
